    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is the 15 July 2026 Jurong East to Changi T1 trip (TRP-00105), charged at SGD 65.13. The GPS trace does show a real and material route deviation, but the driver's explanation for it cannot be tested on this record. Under POL-RD-10 the case goes to a human reviewer and the SGD 65.13 is held — neither collected nor refunded — until it can be decided. Escalation is terminal and replaces any monetary ruling.\n\nWhat is established. EV-GPS-00105 records 54.16 km driven between the recorded pickup and the recorded dropoff against the platform optimal of 36.0 km on EV-TRIP-00105: an excess of 18.16 km, 50.44% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (over 0.8 km, over 20%) and both materiality thresholds (over 8.0 km, over 50%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. I use the trace figure, not the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km. The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 427 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0 — so no corroboration is needed for the deviation itself.\n\nWhy the case cannot be finally decided (POL-RD-10(5)). The driver's only account is 'traffic was heavy on the PIE so I used another way'. That is an exculpatory explanation turning on the road conditions, and the artifact the policy requires to test it — a traffic_advisory under POL-RD-03, naming a road the optimal route uses over the trip window — is absent from the bundle: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is a MISSING artifact with no payload and weight 0.0. An exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool is a mandatory escalation trigger under POL-RD-10(5), which names this exact posture ('a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory'). Both advocates argued the advisory point, but the referee discarded each of those claims for citing the 0.0-weight artifact without disclosing its impairment and issue code (MISSING_ARTIFACT); the trigger therefore rests on the clause and the record alone, not on any advocate claim.\n\nWhat would resolve it. The LTA traffic advisory — or any independent record of the road conditions — for the PIE eastbound and the alternative corridor actually driven, between 14:26 and 15:44 on 15 July 2026. With that artifact in the pool, POL-RD-03 could be run or dismissed and the fare question decided.\n\nPoints the reviewer will need. (a) No rider-requested detour: EV-CHAT-00105 carries no detour instruction and every message has waypoint_hint null, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run. (b) No endpoint amendment: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. (c) vehicle_type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. (d) No pass-through lines: ERP is 0.00 and the airport surcharge is 0.00 (correctly — the trip terminates at Changi and does not originate there). (e) On the money otherwise in issue: charged_total 65.13; POL-RD-02 recomputed_fare 43.36 (base 3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min, surge 1.0 read from EV-FARE-00105, + 0.80 platform fee); POL-RD-02 partial 21.80. (f) A repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06 — deviation_flags_90d = 4 against a threshold of 3 — on EV-DPROF-00105, which is impaired (STALE_SNAPSHOT: snapshot 108 hours before the filing against a 72-hour threshold) at weight multiplier 0.75; the counter survives that discount, and I do not use prior_deviation_flags, a lifetime counter that is context-only under POL-GEN-01. (g) The rider's own profile is clean and was not used against him. Confidence is capped at 0.75, the weight of the impaired profile that carries the pattern finding."
  },
